feat: doodle texture behind the gallery canvas

Carries the hero's treatment onto the gallery, which was a plain white
field behind the scattered photographs.

The layer is extracted into a shared DoodleField rather than copied.
Opacity and tile size are the whole treatment and both are easy to get
subtly wrong in a duplicate, so the hero and the gallery now read from
one definition.

Three surfaces on the gallery carry it: the desktop canvas, the mobile
static hero, and the placeholder that renders before the viewport has
been measured — that last one so the texture is present from the first
paint rather than appearing once the branch is picked.

The desktop canvas gains its own stacking context and the texture sits
at z-0 beneath the world, which is otherwise unlayered.

Verified at 1440 and 390: the layer spans the full viewport height on
both, tiles at 547px and 340px, and paints at 34.7% and 25.2% coverage.
No overflow, no console errors, no failed requests.
